  "question": {
    "text": "If the electric flux entering and leaving an enclosed surface respectively is $\\phi_1$ and $\\phi_2$, the electric charge inside the surface will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "zznbh",
      "text": "\n$\\left(\\phi_2-\\phi_1\\right) \\varepsilon_0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "8mfXr",
      "text": "\n$\\left(\\phi_1+\\phi_2\\right) / \\varepsilon_0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "62bc1",
      "text": "\n$\\left(\\phi_2-\\phi_1\\right) / \\varepsilon_0$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ucpdn",
      "text": "\n$\\left(\\phi_1+\\phi_2\\right) \\varepsilon_0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "According to Gauss's Law\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\int(\\text { E.dA })=\\mathrm{q}_0 / \\varepsilon_0 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{q}=\\varepsilon_0\\left(\\phi_2-\\phi_1\\right) \\\\\n& {\\left[\\text { since } \\phi=\\int \\mathrm{E} \\cdot \\mathrm{dA}\\right]}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
